  "caption": "Nephew Max, 13, lives for basketball. Lately one knee aches deep inside after games and sometimes catches. Everyone says growing pains.\n\nActivity-linked knee pain in one knee of a teen can sometimes be osteochondritis dissecans, a spot under the joint surface. Growing knees often heal well, so it's worth not brushing off as growing pains.\n\nWhat can help: noting the pattern, getting persistent pain reviewed (an X-ray is often the first step), a physio-guided period of reduced load with low-impact alternatives, keeping the coach in the loop, and not rushing back to jumping just because pain settles.\n\nGet it checked for locking, catching, giving way, swelling, a knee that won't straighten, or one-sided pain lasting more than a few weeks.\n\nOur Sydney CBD and Chatswood physios can help. Book via the link in bio.\n\nGeneral information only — not a substitute for an individual assessment.",
